        "original_id": "b01e7bde-39f9-5608-978e-c1a865a35456",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Moe Greene, Moe Dalitz, Hyman Martin\n- Works: The Godfather\n- Topics: Fictional characters, gangsters, mob associates\n\nFacts:\n- Moe Dalitz was the nickname of Morris Barney Dalitz, an American gangster, businessman, casino owner, and philanthropist who lived from December 25, 1899 to August 31, 1989.\n- Hyman Martin, also known as Pittsburgh Hymie, was a Pittsburgh mobster born on April 6, 1903 who was a close associate of Moe Dalitz and Louis Rothkopf.\n- Moe Greene is a fictional character who appears in Mario Puzo's 1969 novel The Godfather and in the 1972 film adaptation of the same name.\n- Hyman Martin died in July 1987.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
